Kcompressd-Unofficial 0.5 for android16-6.12-2025-09 @ 1ad7be92b
Upstream : https://github.com/firelzrd/kcompressd-unofficial
           patches/stable/0001-linux6.12.44-kcompressd-unofficial-0.5.patch (HEAD 3a42168),
           after Kcompressd by Qun-Wei Lin (MediaTek).
GKI KMI  : upstream adds ~64 bytes of per-node state to struct pglist_data, which has one
           8-byte KABI slot and is reachable from a large share of vendor imports. That
           state lives in a side table in mm/swap.h instead; pglist_data is untouched.
Port     : CONFIG_KCOMPRESSD guard (upstream is unconditional); the kthread also wakes
           on kthread_should_stop() (upstream would hang kthread_stop on an empty queue).
Runtime  : vm.kcompressd = queue depth, 0 = off (synchronous, as stock).

